      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient with AMI caused by a large thrombus in the proximal LAD was successfully treated with PTCA and an intracoronary lysis combined with the platelet-receptor antagonist c7E3. Analysis of cellular hemostasis after 1 and 6 months revealed a sustained platelet activation despite combined anti-platelet therapy with ASA and ticlopidine. A progredient slow-flow phenomenon appeared during control angiographies, confirmed by intracoronary Doppler examination."},
